            "text": "{\n  \"judgments\": [\n    {\n      \"proposal_id\": \"P0000\",\n      \"meaning\": {\n        \"source_refs\": [\"F005\"],\n        \"rationale\": \"Subsection (c) expressly establishes an emergency exception making the use of a hand-held mobile telephone permissible by drivers of a CMV when necessary to communicate with law enforcement officials or other emergency services.\",\n        \"verdict\": \"supported\"\n      },\n      \"targets\": [\n        {\n          \"target_alias\": \"C0000\",\n          \"affected_action\": \"Carves out an exception to the prohibition against a driver using a hand-held mobile telephone while driving a CMV, permitting such use when necessary to communicate with law enforcement officials or other emergency services; all other hand-held mobile telephone use while driving remains prohibited.\",\n          \"source_refs\": [\"F002\", \"F005\"],\n          \"rationale\": \"F005 explicitly makes using a hand-held mobile telephone permissible by drivers of a CMV in the specified emergency circumstances, directly qualifying the general driver prohibition established in F002.\",\n          \"verdict\": \"supported\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"target_alias\": \"C0001\",\n          \"affected_action\": \"No change is supported; the prohibition against motor carriers allowing or requiring their drivers to use a hand-held mobile telephone while driving a CMV remains completely unaffected.\",\n          \"source_refs\": [\"F003\", \"F005\"],\n          \"rationale\": \"F005 limits the emergency permission strictly to 'drivers of a CMV' and does not state an exception for motor carriers or authorize motor carriers to allow or require drivers to use hand-held mobile telephones under F003. Applying this qualification to C0001 would wrongly admit motor carriers requiring or directing hand-held phone use in emergencies without source support.\",\n          \"verdict\": \"unsupported\"\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}",
